# History: this file briefly suppressed CVE-2026-5773 and CVE-2026-6276
# (curl/libcurl, HIGH) while the fix (curl 8.20.0-r0+) lagged Alpine's
# v3.23 stable branch. Resolved 2026-07-17 by bumping the base image to
# the Alpine 3.24 line (ghcr.io/linuxserver/baseimage-alpine:3.24-03b33b49-ls6),
# which ships curl 8.21.0-r0 and does not need the ignore. See the FROM
# comment in the Dockerfile for the full record.
#
# 2026-09-08: GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 (msgpack) and CVE-2025-47273 (setuptools)
# are pip 26.2.1's OWN internal vendored copies -- pip/_vendor/msgpack==1.1.2
# and pip/_vendor/setuptools==70.3.0 (confirmed against pip's vendor.txt at
# that exact tag), not the top-level `msgpack`/`setuptools` packages this
# image also installs, which are current (see the venv RUN line in the
# Dockerfile, right after the c-ares/jq/openssl comment). Not reachable at
# runtime: pip is only used during the image build, never invoked by the
# running app (same Dockerfile comment already establishes this for pip
# itself). No pip release has bumped these vendor pins yet as of this date.
# Re-check next time this file changes; drop these two lines once a pip
# release updates its vendored msgpack/setuptools past the fixed versions.
